  "description": "Written by hand, per platform, not recorded: 0.3.0's Copy Command put every argument in plain double quotes and named `<MKVToolNix directory>/mkvextract`; 1.0.0 quotes for the platform's shell (POSIX single quotes; on Windows the Command Prompt and CommandLineToArgvW rules) and names the mkvextract an extraction runs. The MKVToolNix directories do not exist, so the command names `mkvextract` in them as it is. Each case extracts the rows of track_selector.json with these keys, with the Default profile.",
